{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/154655-ink-monkeys-solar-hero-style-questions","id":154655,"title":"Ink monkeys solar hero style questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-31T04:01:29-07:00","id":154655,"title":"Ink monkeys solar hero style questions","content":"Hey guys wondering if you can help me The charms &quot;second impact flourish&quot; and &quot;world rupturing blow&quot; talk about doing &quot;(essence) levels of automatic damage&quot; and &quot;the number of motes spent (max strength) time 3 amount of automatic damage&quot; respectively. How does this automatic damage interact with soak? Is it bypassed, or soaked as normal? Tis confusing cause most the pc and npc are walking around with 15+ soak in our game and would reduce what I assume are meant to be quite powerful charms to 1 die damage (or one level in this case). Thanks for any comments or guidance your guys can give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","user":"Steel_in_sea","date":".  Formatting 05-31-2014, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:04:37-07:00","id":154675,"title":"","content":"Urggggh sorry about crappy formatting iPad won't let me space things out nicely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:28:41-07:00","id":154690,"title":"","content":"I think the they have an Errata for this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dealing Levels of Damage<br /> When effects deal levels of damage, that damage is not rolled, but merely applied as if they were all successes. Soak does apply as normal to this damage, however. The automatic levels are soaked first. So, for example, an attack that is inflicting 10 dice of lethal damage plus five levels of lethal damage going up against a lethal soak of 7 inflicts eight dice of lethal damage: the five automatic levels are soaked first, then the first two dice of damage follow, leaving eight dice of damage.<br /> <br /> If, for example, you have an effect that deals 12 Levels of Damage dealt by a character with Essence 5, who hits someone with a soak of 9, the damage would be soaked down to five dice of damage (Essence ping), by a strict interpretation of the rules. It is a fair approach, however, to permit the damage to be three automatic levels of damage, plus two dice thereof. </div> </div> </div>Reading the above, I think you still soak those level of damage as normal damage dice. So if you deal 5 level of lethal damage again a lethal soak of 4 then they suffer the 1 level of lethal damage, you don't have to roll it at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:34:50-07:00","id":154697,"title":"","content":"Thanks Is that old errata? Cause I didn't think essence ping existed any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:59:02-07:00","id":154703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steel_in_sea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/154655-ink-monkeys-solar-hero-style-questions?p=154697#post154697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Is that old errata? Cause I didn't think essence ping existed any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so, the minimum damage is one dice now instead of (Essence). So in the second example from the errata, it's only 3 automatic level of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 05-31-2014, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298